{
  "meta": {
    "name": "Symphonica Design System",
    "version": "1.0.0",
    "mode": "base",
    "description": "Core, semantic and component tokens aligned with current Figma variables. Alerts, badges, filled, outlined and icon buttons are connected through semantic aliases.",
    "llmImplementationNotes": {
      "buttonOutlinedInteraction": "Outlined labeled buttons and outlined icon-only (card header) buttons: default state uses background, foreground, border. For hover and active, use the nested tokens component.button.outlined.[primary|danger|success].hover|active.(background|border|foreground). Background and border share the same semantic.action.* color (solid fill). Foreground aliases to the matching filled variant foreground (white on brand) for contrast. For disabled, use the nested .disabled object: background stays white, border and foreground use the semantic.action.*.disabled token. Do not apply semantic.action hover colors only to text/border while keeping a white background. Does not apply to table tbody Actions columns: those use circular component.button.icon variants only (never outlined icon-only there); row-level affordance timing follows tableActionColumnRowHoverVisibility.",
      "buttonIconCircularSurfaces": "Default circular icon buttons (component.button.icon.primary|danger) use neutral white hover background for table rows and similar dense rows on secondary app background. Inside Primary or Secondary card bodies (white card surface), use variant tokens component.button.icon.primaryCard or .dangerCard: hover background is semantic.color.secondary so the affordance reads on white without a harsh white chip. Table action columns and table footer load-more must keep the default variant, not primaryCard. In tbody Actions cells, whether the buttons are shown at all follows tableActionColumnRowHoverVisibility (row hover / focus-within); once visible, per-button hover still uses this default-variant behavior (e.g. white chip).",
      "tableActionColumnRowHoverVisibility": "Table body Actions column only (not footer load-more): circular icon buttons hidden by default; show on tbody row hover and on row :focus-within for keyboard. Use opacity plus Core/Motion tokens for transition; do not animate display. Respect prefers-reduced-motion. Pointer-events coordination while hidden is implementation detail; keep controls in tab order. Canonical detail: Symphonica_design.md section 5.4, Table Action Column, Row hover visibility.",
      "navTabsTopSecondaryCards": "Inside Secondary Card bodies, section switching uses Bootstrap nav.nav-tabs structure with class sym-nav-tabs-top. Tokens live under component.nav.tabs.top (track border, tab typography/spacing, inactive/inactiveHover/active/disabled). Inactive tab borders are transparent (no box). inactiveHover MUST use primary border on top/left/right (component.nav.tabs.top.inactiveHover.borderColor) plus borderBottomCover matching the hover background (neutral.100) so the tab edge masks the track—do not reuse inactive.borderColor on hover or the border stays invisible. Active tab: white background, primary border, borderBottomCover white, semantic.text.title. Track: bottom border primary. See Figma Bootstrap UI Kit tabs-top. Do not use Pills for this pattern inside secondary cards.",
      "symphonicaAppSidebar": "Primary app navigation is the Symphonica sidebar (Guía de Estilos). Reference: https://www.figma.com/design/7JdlMVI0UphCTyuHFF9Fww/Guia-de-Estilos-de-Symphonica?node-id=7089-7392 Use component.nav.sidebar tokens only (expanded width aliases layout.apiExplorer.sidebarColumnWidth 330px; collapsed 64px). White surface, vertical padding px/py from tokens, Material Icons Outlined 24px leading per row, labels Montserrat 14 medium semantic.text.primary, trailing chevron_right in neutral.500. Vertical spacing between nav rows: menuListGap MUST be Core/Spacing/24 (24px clear between leading icons—use itemPaddingY 0 so gap is not inflated). Search row: 16px placeholder neutral.600, border neutral.400 (Bootstrap text field pattern). Horizontal gap icon–label: itemGap 16. Collapsed: hide labels/chevrons and search; center icons; no scrollbar on sidebar (overflow hidden on shell and nav); toggle menu_open (expanded) / menu (collapsed). Expanded: scroll only the nav list if needed, not the whole aside. Wordmark \"Symphonica\" uses semantic.text.title weight semibold for showcase; production may swap asset.",
      "cardNesting": "Never nest a Primary Card inside a Secondary Card. The only allowed card-in-card pattern is Secondary inside Primary (e.g. detail clusters inside a main module). When a Secondary Card is nested inside a Primary Card body, set its default surface background to component.card.secondary.nestedInPrimary.background (alias Core/LegacyNeutral/Subtle), not white on white. Standalone Secondary cards on the app secondary background keep component.card.secondary.default.background (white). Borders and Secondary states (hover/active/selected/grid) are unchanged unless the spec adds nested variants."
    }
  },
  "principles": {
    "clarity_over_creativity": true,
    "explicit_feedback": true,
    "strict_figma_consistency": true,
    "token_driven": true,
    "no_hardcoded_values": true,
    "prefer_aliases_over_duplication": true,
    "preserve_backward_compatibility": true
  },
